  "description": "Proposed Works – First‑Floor Side Extension\n1. New First‑Floor Side Extension\nLocation: Above the existing single-storey on the side (north-east elevation), forming a new room at first-floor level.\n\nSize & Position:\nSet back from the front wall of the house by approximately  m, ensuring the extension appears subordinate.\nRoof ridge lowered by approximately 0.3–0.5 m below the main house ridge to reduce bulk and preserve the original profile.\n\n2. Roof Design\nA pitched roof matching the angle and design of the existing house, maintaining architectural harmony.\nAll roof materials (tiles, eaves, fascias) match the existing structure for visual consistency.\n\n3. Wall Finishes & Window Design\nExternal walls rendered and painted to match existing.\nWindows arranged with consistent style and proportions:\nOne first-floor window on the new side elevation.\nAll windows have matching frames, leads, and sill details.\n\n4. Impact on No. 30 Gould Road\nThe extension is stepped-in and set-back to ensure it does not intrude upon the 45-degree sightline from No. 30’s main rear living window.\nThe lowered ridge and boundary separation reduce any sense of enclosure or overbearing.\n\n5. Internal Layout Adjustments\nSide room added upstairs, accessible from the existing landing area.\nGround floor remains intact with no structural changes at ground level.\n\n6. Compliance with Regulations\nExtension materials, scale, and massing align with the Hounslow Residential Extension SPD and Local Plan Policies CC1, CC2, and SC7.\nDesign ensures subordination in scale, visual harmony, and neighbour protection.",
